license: MIT
date-released: "2026-11-14"
keywords:
  - floating-point reproducibility
  - GPU atomic operations
  - scatter-add
  - deterministic parallel reduction
  - commutative monoid
abstract: >-
  Confluent Accumulation Cells (CAC) make floating-point scatter-add independent of
  execution order with two to four 64-bit cells per destination, in one pass and with
  no prior knowledge of the value range. This repository contains the C++17 reference
  model, the experiments, the results and the paper.
